    "title": "Three Journalists Killed in Gaza Airstrike",
    "text": "• An Israeli airstrike in Gaza killed three journalists on Wednesday.\n• One of the journalists, Abed Shaat, was a cameraman who worked for CBS News and other outlets.\n• The other two journalists were identified as Mohammed Salah Qashta and Anas Ghneim.\n• The airstrike occurred in the Al-Zahra area, southwest of Gaza City.\n• The Israel Defense Forces (IDF) stated they targeted suspects operating a Hamas-affiliated drone.\n• An eyewitness reported the journalists were using a drone to film aid distribution when the strike occurred.\n• The Egyptian Relief Committee confirmed one of its vehicles was targeted, resulting in three deaths.\n• Abed Shaat had been working with the Egyptian Humanitarian Committee, photographing humanitarian activities.\n• Abed Shaat was 30 years old and had been married for two weeks.\n• The Palestinian Journalists' Syndicate condemned the strike.\n• The Gaza health ministry reported at least 466 Palestinians have been killed since the ceasefire.\n• The Israeli military reported three soldiers killed during the same period.\n• The Gaza health ministry reported eight other Palestinians were killed in attacks on Wednesday.",
